## On the job {.unnumbered}

::: callout-important
## Why this matters day to day

This is the checklist to pin up. Almost every analysis you're asked to
do is a version of "pick the model that matches the outcome, state
your assumptions, check your work, report uncertainty honestly." Doing
that consistently — and being able to explain each step in one
sentence — is what makes an analysis something a stakeholder can act
on rather than something they have to take on faith.
:::

